 "text": "Population of Costa Rica 1950-2026 & Future Projections\n\nReal Time Statistics\n\nLoading data ... Net population growth so far this year\n\nLoading data ... Deaths so far today\n\nAs of July 1, 2025, Costa Rica's population was 5,152,950, representing approximately 0.06% of the total world population. Among them, 2,545,669 were males and 2,607,282 were females. Overall, the population grew by 0.435%, reflecting an increase of 23,040 people compared to the previous year.\n\nCurrently Costa Rica records a birth every 10.5 minutes, or a total of 138 births per day. At the same time 1 death is recorded every 17.6 minutes, totalling 82 deaths per day. While 1 person immigrates every 9.1 hours leaving the net migration for a day to 3 and the daily net change of the population to 58.\n\n## Historic Population of Costa Rica (1950 - 2025)\n\nBetween 1950 and 2025 the population of Costa Ricagrown from 926,758 people to 5,152,950. An increase of the population size by 456.02% in 75 years.\n\n Date Source: UN World Population Prospects (2024) | License: CCBY | Note: Values indicate mid year (1 July)\n\n| Year | Population | Change +/- | Growth |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| 1950 | 926,758 | 30,762 | 3.32% |\n| 1951 | 958,409 | 32,540 | 3.396% |\n| 1952 | 991,794 | 34,229 | 3.452% |\n| 1953 | 1,027,005 | 36,195 | 3.525% |\n| 1954 | 1,064,119 | 38,031 | 3.574% |\n| 1955 | 1,103,049 | 39,830 | 3.611% |\n| 1956 | 1,143,847 | 41,766 | 3.652% |\n| 1957 | 1,186,633 | 43,807 | 3.692% |\n| 1958 | 1,231,551 | 46,028 | 3.738% |\n| 1959 | 1,278,588 | 48,046 | 3.758% |\n| 1960 | 1,327,496 | 49,770 | 3.75% |\n| 1961 | 1,377,920 | 51,078 | 3.707% |\n| 1962 | 1,429,445 | 51,972 | 3.636% |\n| 1963 | 1,481,604 | 52,346 | 3.533% |\n| 1964 | 1,533,960 | 52,366 | 3.414% |\n| 1965 | 1,586,208 | 52,130 | 3.287% |\n| 1966 | 1,638,116 | 51,686 | 3.155% |\n| 1967 | 1,689,523 | 51,127 | 3.026% |\n| 1968 | 1,739,731 | 49,290 | 2.833% |\n| 1969 | 1,789,276 | 49,801 | 2.783% |\n| 1970 | 1,838,